evolution-sieve-filters (0.6.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Leaving the "Server" field empty in the account's "Sieve Filters"
    tab now really uses the receiving (IMAP) server, as the page says:
    the Sieve Filters dialog no longer reports "No ManageSieve server
    configured", and a password entered there is found again when
    connecting. A password saved while the field was empty must be
    entered once more.
  * Accounts using Kerberos (GSSAPI) for IMAP get GSSAPI pre-selected
    as the Sieve authentication type, instead of an automatic check
    that tried password types first.

 -- cyr-ius <cyr-ius@ipocus.net>  Sat, 03 Oct 2026 13:30:00 +0000

evolution-sieve-filters (0.6.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * A rule with a single condition is saved without a redundant
    "allof (...)" around it.
  * Comments before the require line (such as a commented-out older
    require) are kept, and no longer cause a second require line to be
    added.
  * Scripts declaring the older "imapflags" extension keep it for the
    flag actions instead of "imap4flags", which servers such as older
    Cyrus versions reject.

 -- cyr-ius <cyr-ius@ipocus.net>  Sat, 03 Oct 2026 14:00:00 +0000

evolution-sieve-filters (0.6.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Visual editor: vacation auto-replies are now editable, with the
    message, the subject and the number of days between two replies to
    the same sender. Multi-line messages are supported.
  * Visual editor: new actions "Reject with a message", "Set IMAP flags
    (replace)" and "Remove IMAP flag", and a "Keep a copy" option for
    "File into" and "Redirect to".
  * The require line no longer keeps extensions that are not used
    anymore just because the script contains rules the visual editor
    cannot represent: those rules are now analyzed too.

 -- cyr-ius <cyr-ius@ipocus.net>  Sat, 03 Oct 2026 12:35:00 +0000

evolution-sieve-filters (0.5.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Sieve scripts are now read with a full RFC 5228 parser. Multi-line
    "text:" strings (vacation messages...) are handled properly: an
    unbalanced quote inside one no longer forces the whole script into
    raw text mode, and a closing brace inside one no longer swallows the
    next rule. Syntax errors now report their line and column.
  * Visual editor: conditions can be negated ("does not contain", "is
    not", size "is at most" / "is at least"...) and can test whether a
    header exists or not.
  * Rules the visual editor would have silently altered are now kept
    verbatim (locked) instead: setflag, fileinto/redirect :copy,
    fileinto :flags, addflag on a variable, address/envelope tests,
    "true" inside anyof/allof, and an if/elsif/else chain.
  * A grammatically invalid command no longer prevents the rest of the
    script from being edited visually: it is kept verbatim on its own.

 -- cyr-ius <cyr-ius@ipocus.net>  Sat, 03 Oct 2026 12:17:05 +0000

evolution-sieve-filters (0.4.10-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * ManageSieve client: hardened the server response parser. Response
    lines, literals, whole responses and SASL round trips are now bounded,
    and malformed data (NUL bytes, invalid UTF-8, bad base64, unexpected
    LISTSCRIPTS/GETSCRIPT/SASL replies) is rejected as a protocol error
    instead of being guessed at.
  * Fixed GETSCRIPT returning every script with one extra trailing
    newline, and a server error sent as a literal ("NO {N}") leaving a
    stray empty line for the next command.
  * Server error messages now show the server's text rather than the raw
    status line.

 -- cyr-ius <cyr-ius@ipocus.net>  Sat, 03 Oct 2026 11:31:03 +0000

evolution-sieve-filters (0.4.9-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Sieve editor: switching from the raw text tab back to the visual
    editor no longer drops "variables" (or any other extension the
    visual editor doesn't know about) from the script's "require" line
    (#4). "variables" is also added automatically when a value contains
    a "${...}" variable reference, and "encoded-character" for
    "${hex:...}" / "${unicode:...}".

