evolution-sieve-filters (0.4.6-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * "Check Supported Types" in the account editor's Sieve Filters page
    now selects the most secure authentication type that works. The
    "Automatic" entry is gone: when no type is saved yet, the check runs
    by itself when the page opens. The GSSAPI-only options below are
    only shown while GSSAPI is selected.
  * New "Fall back to another type if GSSAPI fails" option (on by
    default): a selected GSSAPI retries once with the next working type
    (e.g. SCRAM with the password) if Kerberos fails, such as with an
    expired ticket.
  * GSSAPI: resolve the server's DNS canonical hostname automatically
    (new "Canonicalize automatically (DNS)" option, on by default), like
    Evolution's own IMAP connector does, so a ManageSieve host reached
    through a DNS alias (CNAME) works without typing the canonical name.
  * Update the French translation.

 -- cyr-ius <cyr-ius@ipocus.net>  Mon, 28 Sep 2026 16:35:47 +0000

evolution-sieve-filters (0.4.5-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix "Check Supported Types" in the account editor's Sieve Filters
    page showing a mechanism struck through (e.g. GSSAPI) although
    "Test" authenticates with it: verdicts from an earlier check are now
    cleared whenever a connection setting changes (including the
    Kerberos hostname), and a successful "Test" un-strikes the mechanism
    it used. When GSSAPI fails, the reason is shown in the button's
    tooltip.
  * Update the French translation.

 -- cyr-ius <cyr-ius@ipocus.net>  Mon, 28 Sep 2026 15:45:44 +0000

evolution-sieve-filters (0.4.4-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix fileinto to a nested folder being rejected by Dovecot when its
    IMAP namespace separator isn't '/' (often '.' for Maildir++), e.g.
    "Name must not have '/' characters" (issue #3). Add a "Folders"
    section to the account editor's Sieve Filters page: a per-account
    "Folder separator" field, with a "Detect Automatically" button that
    asks the account's real IMAP server directly (there is no public
    Camel/EDS API exposing it) and reuses its stored password; not
    available for OAuth2 accounts. fileinto paths are translated
    between the visual editor's canonical '/' and this separator when
    switching between the visual and raw text tabs.
  * Update the French translation.

 -- cyr-ius <cyr-ius@ipocus.net>  Sun, 27 Sep 2026 11:21:55 +0000

evolution-sieve-filters (0.4.3-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix SASL GSSAPI against a ManageSieve server reached through a DNS
    alias (CNAME), when the server expects a different Kerberos service
    principal than the one built from the connection host (issue #2).
    Add an optional "Kerberos hostname:" field to the account editor's
    Authentication section (and --gssapi-hostname to test-managesieve)
    to override the hostname used to build the GSSAPI service principal
    ("sieve/<hostname>"); empty by default, using the connection host as
    before.
  * Update the French translation.

 -- cyr-ius <cyr-ius@ipocus.net>  Sun, 27 Sep 2026 10:09:05 +0000

evolution-sieve-filters (0.4.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add a "Type" list to the Authentication section of the account
    editor's Sieve Filters page, to force a SASL mechanism (default:
    Automatic). The choice is stored per account and used by the "Test"
    button and by the editing dialog.
  * Add a "Check Supported Types" button that tries each mechanism and
    strikes through those that do not work. Password/OAuth failures are
    only counted against a mechanism if another one succeeded, and the
    check stops after two such failures, so a wrong password cannot lock
    the account.
  * Update the French translation.

 -- cyr-ius <cyr-ius@ipocus.net>  Sun, 20 Sep 2026 13:15:26 +0000

evolution-sieve-filters (0.4.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix SASL GSSAPI locking users out: automatic negotiation picks
    GSSAPI as soon as a Kerberos ticket exists, but it can still fail
    (service principal missing from the server's keytab, CNAME or
    canonicalization mismatch), and there was no fallback. A failed
    GSSAPI attempt now falls back to the next mechanism (SCRAM, PLAIN…).
    Only GSSAPI in automatic mode is retried: password mechanisms are
    never replayed and a forced mechanism is never replaced.

 -- cyr-ius <cyr-ius@ipocus.net>  Sun, 20 Sep 2026 12:54:01 +0000

evolution-sieve-filters (0.4.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add an "Unlock" button to an opaque rule's read-only view in the
    visual editor: reinterprets its raw text as conditions/actions
    (same grammar as a normal rule, without requiring the leading
    "# rule:[name]" marker), typically after fixing it up in the "Raw
    text" tab. On failure the rule is left untouched and the reason is
    shown inline.
  * Add "move up" / "move down" buttons to the visual editor's rule
    list, to reorder rules without going through the raw text tab.
    Rule order is significant in Sieve (top-to-bottom evaluation,
    "stop" short-circuits the rest); works for opaque rules too.

 -- cyr-ius <cyr-ius@ipocus.net>  Sun, 13 Sep 2026 12:54:46 +0000

evolution-sieve-filters (0.3.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix several data-corruption bugs in the visual/raw editor: a
    ":regex" match type was silently downgraded to ":contains", a value
    list with more than one entry (e.g. ["a", "b"]) was truncated to
    its first element, and a disabled "if false" test was
    re-serialized as "if true", inverting the rule's logic. Any
    construct the editor can't safely represent now falls back to a
    read-only "opaque" copy instead of being silently mangled.
  * Add ":regex" as a supported match type in the visual editor
    (requires the Sieve "regex" extension on the server).
  * Add support for multi-value conditions (a Sieve string list, e.g.
    matching several senders at once): editable as a comma-separated
    field, with "\," / "\\" escaping for a literal comma or backslash
    within a value.
  * Add per-rule enable/disable in the visual editor. A disabled rule
    is saved as "if false # <test>", the same convention used by
    Roundcube's managesieve plugin, so the original test survives
    re-enabling and stays compatible with scripts managed by other
    Sieve tools.

 -- cyr-ius <cyr-ius@ipocus.net>  Sun, 13 Sep 2026 12:27:01 +0000

evolution-sieve-filters (0.2.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add SASL GSSAPI (Kerberos) authentication support: automatic
    mechanism negotiation now picks GSSAPI when the caller has a usable
    Kerberos ticket (e.g. an Active Directory-joined workstation),
    falling back to SCRAM/PLAIN/etc. otherwise; --mech GSSAPI forces it
    explicitly. New optional build dependency on libkrb5, used only to
    detect a usable ticket for automatic negotiation.

